	(text "Physical matrix, scanned by the MCU at 3.3 V: 6 rows x 20 columns following the board (pcb/tools/layout.py\nphysical_matrix), not the C128's assignment; the firmware maps each position to its host position.  One diode per\nkey (row -> switch -> diode -> column) so any chord reads without ghosting: needed for USB keyboard mode.  RESTORE\nbypasses the MCU entirely.  Columns 0-14 straight from the 74HC154 (3.3 V; output 15 is the idle park), 15-19\nstraight from GPIO.  No series resistors: a column held high reverse-biases its diodes, so two keys in one row\ncannot connect two outputs."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15.24 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d94185fa-7143-518d-a6f9-89eb90e5f81c")
	)
